#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:5
#: e1b579ae224f466ba777f392cc98b7bb
msgid "Manual tuning of Roll and Pitch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:7
#: f49e6fcd2d9044198b9e726c3e3049c9
msgid "Manual tuning may be required to provide a stable tune before Autotune is run, or if Autotune does not produce an acceptable tune. The process below can be done on roll and pitch at the same time for a quick manual tune **provided the aircraft is symmetrical**. If the aircraft is not symmetrical, then the process should be done for roll and pitch individually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:9
#: 2ba6ecebbeec43e3a05e7d18ead07105
msgid "The pilot should be especially careful to ensure that :ref:`ATC_THR_MIX_MAN <ATC_THR_MIX_MAN>` and :ref:`MOT_THST_HOVER <MOT_THST_HOVER>` are set correctly before manual tuning is started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:11
#: 512d4d9694674e66b70b4853f8e7e59f
msgid "When oscillations start do not make large or sudden stick inputs. Reduce the throttle smoothly to land the aircraft while using very slow and small roll and pitch inputs to control the aircraft position. For each axis:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:14
#: c21e852edd33456485c7c050e3e0e76d
msgid "If the vehicle already oscillates in an axis, first lower the P, D, and I terms in 50% steps until stable, before starting manual tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:16
#: 629f45f4975940bfa036a4328cdabbfc
msgid "Increase the D term in steps of 50% until oscillation is observed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:17
#: bfc8505ad7bf4ee6bebf3da9fb2b35e4
msgid "Reduce the D term in steps of 10% until the oscillation disappears"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:18
#: e02311efaa174aff8dbb885ab347a238
msgid "Reduce the D term by a further 25%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:19
#: 225a288597e24998a907ef4df901811b
msgid "Increase the P term in steps of 50% until oscillation is observed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:20
#: f84fe1b7b54a430ea4ca0c1dcfab2215
msgid "Reduce the P term in steps of 10% until the oscillation disappears"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:21
#: 973574782f0c4d9a9c6ba91c7db69e93
msgid "Reduce the P term by a further 25%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:23
#: fdf95bde03f84db7abb8ce285973d9ef
msgid "Each time the P term is changed set the I term equal to the P term. Those parameters can be changed on ground and preferably disarmed. A confident pilot could set them in flight with GCS or transmitter tuning knob (see :ref:`Transmitter based tuning<common-transmitter-tuning>` page for setup of this feature)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:27
#: b6f78e6f6cc64646a12f2f83aa5541c9
msgid "If using :ref:`Transmitter based tuning<common-transmitter-tuning>`, set the minimum value of the tuning range to the current safe value and the upper range to approximately 4 times the current value. Be careful not to move the slider before the parameter list is refreshed to recover the set value. Ensure the transmitter tuning is switched off before setting the parameter value or the tuning may immediately overwrite it."
msgstr ""

